    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Riders With A Passenger Rental Paperwork Questions</h1>
    <p>Rental paperwork is where a conversation becomes an agreement, and when two people will share the machine, the paper needs to say what two people actually agreed to. Most rental slips are written for a rider, so a pair needs the same slip to honestly cover the second helmet, the second person belongings and the second set of expectations. The fix is not a different document, it is a better set of questions, asked before the pen moves, with both riders standing at the counter.</p>
    <p>This page is the paperwork chapter of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster for riders with a passenger. The verified fleet prices are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, general questions are on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, the machine-matching chapter is the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/riders-with-a-passenger-bike-choice/">bike-choice page</a>, and the full general question set is listed in the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/how-to-rent-a-motorbike-in-hanoi/">how-to-rent guide</a>.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Why two riders change the paperwork questions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The documents the counter records</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Questions about the second helmet and accessories</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Deposits, holds and what secures what</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Reading the condition slip as a pair</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-6">Rental terms worth asking out loud</a></li>
